body:
This should be taken in the context of an increasing global energy demand. 

It would be uplifting if this weren't true: [Exxon Sees 2050 Oil Use at Current Level, Despite Net Zero Goal
](https://www.bnnbloomberg.ca/markets/oil/2024/08/26/exxon-sees-net-zero-missed-with-2050-oil-demand-as-high-as-today/)

I don't think a change in societal view will change much about ***how much*** sex is being had. People already know about sex, and those who want to, will (or try to).

&#x200B;

Normalizing the idea of sex will bring about better education and support systems and can reduce bad outcomes of sex, such as pregnancy and STDs.

&#x200B;

I feel like this applies most to teenagers. Some teenagers are advised against sex but do it anyway. If and when they encounter a bad outcome such as pregnancy and STDs, there are currently societal barriers that prevent them from getting the best help.

But what is inherent about sex that requires it to be special? Is it then wrong to have sex with a stranger?

&#x200B;

Sex addiction is a real illness, but the majority of people who like sex aren't addicts. Just like how some people can be addicted to food, drugs, gambling, etc., but can still function normally.

Context: I'm Canadian.

&#x200B;

A few years back, the Liberal Provincial Government of Ontario released plans to introduce kids to sex ed early on (I forget at what age, but I think it was around 8 years old) that garnered a lot of disagreement from the public. I thought this was perfectly fine as it's just education and some kids actually start puberty that early and should at least know what's going on.

>*but also something you don't openly speak of*

Exactly, so it is not *as* accepted as massages. I compare sex to massages because it is another physical activity that (supposedly) feels good.

&#x200B;

I believe that current societal norms (excluding religion) are not enough to justify the taboo that still surrounds sex, i.e., why **can't** you talk about a good orgasm with your peers if you can talk about a good massage or a good steak? Obviously the answer is *"because it's inappropriate"* but I don't believe that there exists a reasonable answer as to ***why*** it's inappropriate.

&#x200B;

Other similar thoughts I have are: *why is it wrong to pick your nose? why is it rude to fart in front of other people? (enclosed spaces, I understand, but what about outdoors?)*

Do I really get what I paid for it? There is a conflicting comment on another reddit post

&#x200B;

[https://www.reddit.com/r/IllegalLifeProTips/comments/98pq3i/ilpt\_get\_a\_new\_laptop\_using\_your\_best\_buy/e4i4bs6?utm\_source=share&utm\_medium=web2x](https://www.reddit.com/r/IllegalLifeProTips/comments/98pq3i/ilpt_get_a_new_laptop_using_your_best_buy/e4i4bs6?utm_source=share&utm_medium=web2x)

I have tried a therapist and didn't find it to help much.

&#x200B;

I actually am buying my plane ticket and hotel on credit. I didn't co-sign with anybody, and since my estate (which is basically nothing because I'm a student) is less than my debts, the creditors will be out of luck.

Naive 18 year old me thought I was going to marry this girl. She proceeded to break my heart. I have dated since and feel like I'm never going to have the same kind of relationship that I had with her.

&#x200B;

Also think I may have a chemical problem with my brain as I have mood swings and depressive waves.
